    36	Matched difference = first − second arm in ms (+ = second arm faster). Per repeat: median of 50 block latencies of arm A minus the same for arm B, blocks alternating in one process after a joint settle. Primary statistic: median over restarts of the per-restart median of the per-repeat differences. Interval: two-level cluster bootstrap (restart, then repeat; 10,000 resamples) of that same statistic (`fullmodel/stats_v2.py`); the historical pooled-repeat interval is also stored next to it but never used for a verdict. Eligibility: registered protocol 5×50, validation PASS at the arm's tier, joint settle affirmatively stable for two rounds, one session manifest, clock-flagged repeats excluded (≥ 1 clean repeat per restart required). Smallest meaningful difference: 0.30 ms at 4/6/8 s, 0.10 ms at 1 s and 100 ms. Verdict rule (plan line 21, implemented in `fullmodel/session4_result.py`): "second (or first) arm faster" when the interval excludes zero and |point| ≥ threshold; "practical tie" when the interval lies inside ±threshold; otherwise "unresolved". Three restarts (two for C1P→C1, one for each A/A) carry the between-restart information; the interval resamples restarts and then repeats, so it is wider than the restart-median range where within-restart variation is large (PC1 at 8 s: restart range [−0.214, −0.154], interval [−0.329, −0.049]).
