   105	
   106	What freezing removes and changes (C3I → C3G, same in the C3 → C3G view): the 420 parameter-cast kernels (0.92 ms at 8 s, 0.86 ms at 100 ms) disappear; the rotary cos/sin are folded (the fused SDPA-side signature `…add,cos,mul,sin` is replaced by `…add,mul` at equal time, 1.36 → 1.39 ms at 8 s); the norm+cast kernels shrink by 0.35 ms at 8 s; the launch count falls by 413 per pass. What freezing costs: the GEMM class is slower after freezing, by 0.13 ms at 8 s and by **0.37 ms at 100 ms** — at 100 ms the GEMM slow-down offsets 44 % of the cast saving in device time, which is why the device-time class sum (0.48) is well below the cast time removed (0.86). The device-time class sums (1.14 ms at 8 s, 0.48 ms at 100 ms) are smaller than the unprofiled wall gains (1.30, 0.74); the gap (≈ 0.16 and ≈ 0.26 ms) is not assigned to anything here. The launch-count reduction (413 fewer graph nodes per pass) is a candidate, but the Phase-3 boundary-bench slopes (0.568 µs/node for a trivial PDL graph, 0.719 µs/node for a trivial graph) are total service times including kernel execution, so they cannot be added to device-time deltas without double counting; no such addition is made and the gap stays unresolved. Inlining off alone changes almost nothing in device time (+0.06 ms class sum at 8 s; +0.06 ms on the GELU kernel) while costing 0.2 ms of wall time; that wall cost is not visible in the traces and stays unresolved. HG (192 kernels per pass, 0 casts, 64 extern GEMMs) and C3MG (556 kernels, 0 casts, 285 Triton template GEMMs + 15 cuBLAS GEMMs at 8 s; 291 + 14 at 100 ms) are documented as deployed; the comparison with the historical control traces — C3M from session 3 (GPU-7d47d5c2: 178 templates + 145 extern GEMMs at 8 s) and H from the Sep-20 session 2 (GPU-6bf4cb32) — is cross-session and descriptive only: with freezing on the max-autotune base most GEMMs are Triton templates rather than cuBLAS entry points.
