   104	- Conjecture: the crossover comes from the per-band path's launch-floor inefficiency at small M (60 tiny GEMMs per projection, each far below its roofline) versus the batched path's 3.94× FLOP waste that only matters once the batched GEMM is compute-bound.
   105	
   106	### C. Mechanism and competing explanations
   107	1. **Latency-floor vs waste (candidate):** T_band(F) ≈ Σ_bands max(t_floor, FLOPs_i(F)/peak) and T_batched(F) ≈ max(t_floor, 3.94·FLOPs(F)/peak); the difference is concave in F and crosses where the per-band GEMMs leave their floors. Predicts: crossover shifts to smaller F for layouts with less dispersion (lower waste) and to larger F for GPUs with higher per-launch floors.
   108	2. **Alternative — attention/body effects:** the transformer body (SDPA, fused kernels) is identical in both arms (SDPA class 3.65–3.69 ms at 8 s in all traces), so it does not drive the difference; ruled out descriptively.
