    10	- **Cost.** Two 8 s matched processes ≈ 12–15 min on GPU 4; no pod.
    11	
    12	## Probe B1 — GEMM operand locality after cast removal (candidate B)
    13	
    14	- **Question.** Do the model's small-M GEMMs at the 100 ms operating point run slower after pre-casting/freezing because the removed cast kernel used to leave the fp16 weight L2-resident (producer-side warming), rather than because a different GEMM kernel is selected?
    15	- **Design.** Capture the (input, weight) shapes of every `nn.Linear` call in one eager forward at chunk 4,410 (hooks). For each distinct shape (weighted by call count), time the GEMM with CUDA events over 200 iterations under four conditions, each preceded by an L2 flush (write 256 MB) so every iteration starts cold: (a) fp32 weight, `.half()` cast kernel immediately followed by the GEMM (the C3 pattern); (b) pre-cast fp16 weight, GEMM alone (the C3P/C3G pattern); (c) pre-cast fp16 weight, a read-only "touch" kernel over the weight immediately before the GEMM (warms L2 without producing the operand); (d) pre-cast fp16 weight, a cast of a *different* fp32 tensor of the same size immediately before the GEMM (same extra work, no warming of the operand). GEMM kernel names and durations from `torch.profiler` (CUDA activities) on a separate short run.
