171. **BLOCKER — [RESEARCH_DIRECTIONS.md:63](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/RESEARCH_DIRECTIONS.md:63), also PROBES.md:7 and PILOT_RESULTS.md:21.** The exhausted frame is **`Attention.forward`**, not the model’s top-level forward. In the [pinned source](https://github.com/ZFTurbo/Music-Source-Separation-Training/blob/ea7eb9c20ea0e3f94368a30fc1654b51cdd55789/models/bs_roformer/mel_band_roformer.py#L127), the latter starts at line 538. The 60/801 dimensions arise from frequency/time attention, not different validation lengths. Furthermore, [PyTorch 2.8’s fallback](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/v2.8.0/torch/_dynamo/convert_frame.py#L1271) permits reuse of compiled nested entries rather than newly compiling nested frames. **Minimal fix:** correct the frame identity and fallback description throughout; retain the observed recompile-budget intervention result.

172. **BLOCKER — [RESEARCH_DIRECTIONS.md:42](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/RESEARCH_DIRECTIONS.md:42), closing inference at line 151.** The proposed pre-hook does not ensure that it touches the GEMM operand. C3G retains fp32 module parameters while its generated GEMMs consume separately materialized fp16 `_frozen_param*` constants. Reading `nn.Linear.weight` can therefore warm different storage. A null result would not establish failure to transfer to graph replay. **Minimal fix:** require the touch to read the actual frozen fp16 operand and verify its placement before interpreting recovery or non-recovery.

173. **BLOCKER — [RESEARCH_DIRECTIONS.md:42](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/RESEARCH_DIRECTIONS.md:42).** Touching every Linear call requires **300 touches**, not 60. Using the document’s own 2 µs assumption gives **0.60 ms**, not 0.12 ms—exceeding the anticipated 0.30 ms GEMM recovery and reversing the predicted net wall-time benefit. **Minimal fix:** correct the launch budget, or explicitly restrict the intervention and expected recovery to a specified subset.

174. **BLOCKER — [RESEARCH_DIRECTIONS.md:107](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/RESEARCH_DIRECTIONS.md:107).** The model does not imply the stated concavity or crossover direction. Once the batched term is linear, individual GEMMs leaving their floors increase the slope of `T_band − T_batched`, contradicting global concavity. Holding other terms fixed, reducing padding makes batching cheaper and delays its loss of advantage; it does not move that crossover earlier. At equal widths, the model also permits a compute-bound **tie**, contrary to “batched always wins” at line 113. **Minimal fix:** correct these deductions and distinguish observed curve shape from a conjectured model.

175. **BLOCKER — [RESEARCH_DIRECTIONS.md:122](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/RESEARCH_DIRECTIONS.md:122), related claim at line 108.** Kernel identity cannot discriminate padding waste from selection here. Existing C3MG traces already contain Triton projection kernels while HG uses cuBLAS/CUTLASS; C3MG also enables max-autotune while HG does not. Different kernels are therefore compatible with the waste mechanism. Equal SDPA totals likewise do not establish equality of the remaining transformer body. **Minimal fix:** withdraw the identical-kernel/3.9× timing criterion and limit the body exclusion to what the traces actually establish.

